# File: tests/features/add_greeting_shake_128_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/296-add-greeting-shake-128-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Return the SHAKE-128 hex digest of the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Return the 32-byte SHAKE-128 hex digest of the greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_shake_128 is called with Ada and Zo plus U+00EB
    Then the results are a3930308111b74c13946954b166ee4057689ba55b2b95de0cebdf8f299818774 and 8479a68098ec2f7e622cd2c40a917d3a8b79221a308ebde33c5825dc6f0b4b3f
    And each result is 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters equal to the 32-byte SHAKE-128 hex digest of the UTF-8 greeting

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_shake_128 is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper without changing the CLI
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_shake_128 of Ada
    Then it prints a3930308111b74c13946954b166ee4057689ba55b2b95de0cebdf8f299818774 and greeting_shake_128 is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And the README documents the fixed 32-byte SHAKE-128 hex output over the UTF-8 greeting and the inherited invalid-name error
    And nmg-smoke Ada still prints exactly Hello, Ada and exits with status 0

